# Recruiter AI Assistant (RAG) — Implementation Plan

## Problem Statement

Recruiters on the **Applicants** page need an AI-powered chat assistant that lets them query applicant data using natural language — e.g. *"Who are my strongest Python candidates?"*, *"Compare the top 3 applicants for the React Developer role"*, *"Which candidates have 5+ years of experience?"*.

---

## Architecture Decision: Vector DB (Pinecone/ChromaDB) vs. Context-Window Stuffing

Before writing any code, here is the core trade-off:

### Option A — Traditional Vector DB RAG (Pinecone / ChromaDB)

| Pros | Cons |
|------|------|
| Scales to thousands of applicants | Adds a new infrastructure dependency (Pinecone cloud or ChromaDB server) |
| Semantic search is very precise | Requires a separate embeddings pipeline (OpenAI/Gemini embeddings API) |
| Industry-standard RAG pattern | Embedding sync must run on every applicant create/update/delete |
| | Adds **significant** operational complexity for a feature that queries a bounded, recruiter-scoped dataset |
| | Pinecone costs money; ChromaDB requires Python + server or JS client with limited support |

### Option B — Context-Window Stuffing with Gemini (Recommended ✅)

| Pros | Cons |
|------|------|
| **Zero new infrastructure** — uses the Gemini API you already have | Won't scale past ~200-300 applicants per query (Gemini's 1M token window handles this easily) |
| No embedding pipeline or sync to maintain | Slightly higher per-query token cost than a vector DB lookup |
| Resume text extraction already exists in [aiService.js](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Backend/services/aiService.js) | N/A for a recruiter's realistic applicant pool |
| Simpler to build, test, and debug | |
| Retrieval is always fresh — reads directly from MongoDB | |

### Why Option B wins for SkillSync

A single recruiter typically has **tens to low-hundreds** of applicants, not millions. Gemini 2.0 Flash has a **1 million token context window** — easily enough to fit all applicant profiles + resume summaries for a recruiter's entire pipeline. Option A adds infrastructure that doesn't solve a problem you actually have.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> If the applicant pool grows past ~500 per recruiter in the future, we can migrate to a vector DB later. The service layer is designed as a clean abstraction, so swapping the retrieval strategy requires changing only `ragService.js`.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Backend

---

#### [NEW] [ragService.js](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Backend/services/ragService.js)

The core RAG service with these responsibilities:

1. **`buildApplicantContext(recruiterId)`** — Fetches all jobs for the recruiter, then all applications for those jobs (with populated user + job data). Extracts resume text for each applicant using the existing [extractTextFromPdf](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Backend/services/aiService.js#14-64) helper from [aiService.js](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Backend/services/aiService.js). Assembles a structured plain-text context document.

2. **`chat(recruiterId, userMessage, conversationHistory)`** — Calls Gemini with a system prompt defining its role as a recruiter assistant + the assembled applicant context + the user's conversation history. Returns the AI response.

Key design decisions:
- Resume text is extracted **on-demand** at query time (cached per session in the future if needed, but Gemini API latency dominates).
- The [extractTextFromPdf](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Backend/services/aiService.js#14-64) function will be refactored out of [aiService.js](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Backend/services/aiService.js) into a shared `pdfUtils.js` so both [aiService.js](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Backend/services/aiService.js) and `ragService.js` can import it without circular dependencies.
- Conversation history is passed from the frontend (stateless on the backend), keeping the API simple and horizontally scalable.

---

#### [NEW] [pdfUtils.js](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Backend/utils/pdfUtils.js)

Extracted [extractTextFromPdf](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Backend/services/aiService.js#14-64) function from [aiService.js](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Backend/services/aiService.js), so it can be shared by both [aiService.js](file:///c:/Users/Computer%20Arena/Documents/webDev%20works/full%20stack/SkillSync/Backend/services/aiService.js) and `ragService.js`.

---

